      "trace_id": "2c85786e03ce152e1698a9a4ee1eb071",
      "output": {
        "question": "what is the sumary of the first book?",
        "answer": "The novel follows disgraced financial journalist Mikael Blomkvist and investigator Lisbeth Salander, who is hired to investigate Blomkvist and notices connections among him, Henrik Vanger and financier Hans-Erik Wennerström. [E1] The central mystery is the disappearance of Henrik’s niece Harriet from Hedeby Island; Henrik believes she was murdered, but she is later revealed to be alive and recently returned from Australia. [c64047bd, b3f28f64, 5e1a7864]",
        "citations": [
          "[E1]"
        ],
        "reranked": [
          {
            "book": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo",
            "book_file": "The Girl with the Dragon Tattoo -- Larsson, Stieg -- Millennium book, 1st Vintage Crime_Black Lizard mass-market -- Random House, Incorporated -- isbn13 9780307455352 -- f10e68d0e06407c85b6ba58f6f49d618 -- Anna’s Archive.epub",
            "section": "The_Girl_with_the_Dragon_Tattoo_split_022.html",
            "paragraph": 169,
            "part": 1,
            "chapter": "CHAPTER 14 Saturday, March 8– Monday, March 17",
            "page": "21",
            "text": "The lawyer Frode from Hedestad had hired her to do an investigation of Mikael Blomkvist, the journalist who was given a prison sentence for libelling financier Hans-Erik Wennerström. A few months later Henrik Vanger, also from Hedestad, joins Blomkvist’s magazine’s board of directors and claims that there is a conspiracy to crush the magazine. All this on the same day that the former goes to prison. Most fascinating of all: a two-year-old background article—“With two empty hands”—about Hans-Erik Wennerström, which she found in the online edition of Monopoly Financial Magazine . It seemed that he began his career in the very same Vanger Corporation in the late sixties.\nYou didn’t have to be a rocket scientist to see that these events were somehow related. There had to be a skeleton in one of their cupboards, and Salander loved hunting skeletons. Besides, she had nothing else on at the moment.",
            "paragraph_end": 170,
            "part_end": 1,
